---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const title = "Our Approach | Cassady Tech Solutions";
const description = "Meet Cassady Tech Solutions and learn how we approach technology operations, cybersecurity, and responsible modernization for small organizations.";
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} active="about">
	<section class="page-title page-title-paper">
		<div class="section-inner page-title-grid">
			<div><p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p><h1>Useful technology starts with paying attention.</h1><p>Cassady Tech Solutions was built around a simple observation: small organizations are often asked to carry enterprise-sized technology decisions without enterprise-sized context.</p></div>
			<div class="quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section founder-section">
		<div class="section-inner founder-grid">
			<div class="founder-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h2>Technology should reduce the number of things a leader has to keep in their head.</h2><p>Sam Cassady built Cassady Tech Solutions to help organizations close the gap between “we have technology” and “we understand the technology we depend on.” The work draws on professional cybersecurity analysis, IT administration, military leadership, and hands-on support for real people with real constraints.</p><p>That background shapes the way we work: steady first, security-aware throughout, and honest about what the current team and budget can maintain.</p></div>
			<aside class="founder-card"><div class="founder-card-top"><span>FOUNDER / PRINCIPAL</span><span class="card-index">SAM</span></div><h3>Sam Cassady</h3><p>Cybersecurity analyst<br />Master's degree in cybersecurity<br />CompTIA Security+ certified<br />U.S. military veteran</p><div class="founder-card-rule"></div><p class="small">Based in Southern Colorado. Working with local organizations and remote-first teams.</p></aside>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section alt-section principles-section">
		<div class="section-inner">
			<div class="section-heading wide-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Working principles</p><h2>How we try to leave things.</h2></div>
			<div class="principle-grid">
				<article><span>01</span><h3>Clearer than before</h3><p>A useful engagement should improve the system and the organization's understanding of it.</p></article>
				<article><span>02</span><h3>Proportionate to the risk</h3><p>Security and resilience matter, but the answer still has to fit the environment and the people maintaining it.</p></article>
				<article><span>03</span><h3>Human where it counts</h3><p>Tools can help with repeatable work. Judgment, accountability, and communication still belong to people.</p></article>
				<article><span>04</span><h3>Honest about boundaries</h3><p>Knowing what is out of scope is part of doing good work, especially with security and AI.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section brand-relationship-section">
		<div class="section-inner brand-relationship-grid">
			<div><p class="eyebrow">One owner, two questions</p><h2>Residential help and organizational work should not sound the same.</h2><p>Greenhorn Valley Tech is the household-facing brand for people and homes. Cassady Tech Solutions is the organizational-facing brand for teams that need technology operations and a thoughtful modernization partner.</p></div>
			<div class="brand-pair"><a href="https://ghvtech.com"><span class="brand-pair-label">Greenhorn Valley Tech</span><strong>Technology for people and homes</strong><span>Local device, Wi-Fi, account, and digital safety help.</span></a><div class="pair-line" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="brand-pair current"><span class="brand-pair-label">Cassady Tech Solutions</span><strong>Technology for organizations</strong><span>Operations, security, automation, and AI enablement.</span></div></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band"><div class="section-inner band-inner"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">No pitch deck required</p><h2>Bring the messy version of the problem.</h2><p>We will help turn it into a clearer technology conversation.</p></div><a class="button button-light" href="/contact">Talk with Cassady Tech</a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
